@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Spec 005: createPatch (JSON Patch generation)
+
+Standards: RFC 6902 (sections 3, 4.1 add, 4.2 remove, 4.3 replace, 4.4 move), RFC 6901 (section 3 and 4: `~0`/`~1` escaping), RFC 8259 (JSON values).
+
+## Request
+`createPatch(from, to)` returns a JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to` through `applyPatch`. Inputs are never mutated.
+
+## Requirements
+- Equal documents (RFC 6902 section 4.6 equality) give `[]`.
+- Minimal: objects are diffed member by member (`add`/`remove`/recursion); a changed primitive or a type change is one `replace`. The whole document is replaced only when its type differs or both are primitives (`replace` with path `""`).
+- Arrays: an inserted/deleted item is one `add`/`remove` at its index; items around it are untouched. A moved item is a `remove` plus an `add` (items in between untouched). Modified items are diffed recursively.
+- Member names are escaped (`~` -> `~0`, `/` -> `~1`); `__proto__` etc. are plain keys.
+- Input that is not a JSON value (RFC 8259) throws `JsonPatchError`. Returned patch shares no structure with the inputs.
+- Array diff is LCS based: O(n*m) time/memory on the part between common prefix and suffix.
+
+## Not in scope
+`copy`/`test` operations, `move` operations (remove+add is allowed by the request).
